WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.979
Clear Rivers was born on September 5th, 1982.

00:00:02.979 --> 00:00:06.669
During her delivery, her real mother passed
away due to childbirth complications, so she

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:07.959
mostly grew up with her father.

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:12.089
He would take her on trips to his waterfront
cabin, teaching her to fish and do other outdoor

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:13.089
activities.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:16.350
Her father did remarry at some point, and
Clear came to love her step-mother.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.440
When she was 6 or 7, she would worry and worry
about her parents dying, so much so that it

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.699
would keep her lying awake at night.

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:26.830
In 1992, when Clear was just 10 years old,
her worst fears came true, when her Dad stepped

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.699
into a 7/11, and an armed robber told him
“don’t turn around.”

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.790
For whatever reason, he did turn around, and
that would be the last thing he ever did.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.760
To learn what happened to Clear in between
Final Destinations 1 and 2, and the details

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.529
added to her backstory in the novelization,
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.810
Welcome to Horror History.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.640
My name is CZsWorld, and I haven’t gotten
a haircut in about a year and half.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.790
Clear Rivers was the first returning character
in the Final Destination franchise and she’s

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.300
also one of the most unique, exhibiting an
ability that no other character seems to possess.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.320
Before we get started, I accidentally got
a second copy of Final Destination on Blu-Ray,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.360
so I’m giving it away.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.610
To enter to win, you just have to be following
me on Instant Grandmother and Like THIS post.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.240
Full rules are in the description.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.770
After losing her father, Clear’s life went
to sh**.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.190
Her step-mother remarried to some asshole
that she never liked when Clear’s real dad

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:28.700
was alive, and the new husband, who is technically
not Clear’s stepfather, didn’t want kids,

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.000
so her stepmother, who technically is still
her stepmother and guardian, began to neglect

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.000
her.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.870
Naturally, this causes Clear to become goth,
just as any kid with a troubled home life

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.020
does in a movie.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.950
But Clear would take it one step further.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:44.979
In 1998, she turned 16 years old, emancipated,
and began living alone in her father’s old

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:45.979
house.

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:49.810
She became an experimental artist and welder,
expressing herself through strange experimental

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.810
art.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.520
She also enjoyed watching crime drama shows.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.140
It’s not clear… no pun intended… if
she made any friends in high school, but it

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.700
would appear that she doesn’t have any friends
in her senior year French class.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.090
She is, however, the most prolific French
speaker in her class.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.981
“Les enfants.

00:02:05.981 --> 00:02:06.692
Ecoutez.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:07.722
Excusez-moi.

00:02:07.722 --> 00:02:08.222
Ecoutez.

00:02:08.656 --> 00:02:10.613
Qu'est ce que c'est I'annonce?”

00:02:11.899 --> 00:02:14.780
“The airport does not endorse solicitors.”

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.120
This is the class’s big end of year field
trip to Paris, France.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.760
The departure date is May 13th, 1999.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.900
Clear mostly has her nose in a book the entire
time, Tropic of Cancer by Henry Miller.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.370
She gets coffee and a snack before boarding,
and at the gate another book falls out of

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.330
her bag, and a classmate named Alex Browning
helps her pick it up.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:35.280
When she takes it, it’s open to a page about
the Princess of Wales dying in a car crash

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.730
in 1997, her first of many ominous signs.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.060
She listens to headphones while boarding,
and is mostly disconnected from the rest of

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.099
the class as she takes her seat in Row 23,
Seat J, where she started to feel a strange

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.710
paranoia, but did not know where the feeling
was coming from.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.350
The next thing she knows, Alex Browning is
having a meltdown, freaking out and yelling

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.250
that the plane is going to explode.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.060
In that moment Clear felt the same uneasiness
that Alex felt, and for whatever reason, she

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.120
believed him and exited the aircraft to sit
alone in the gate area.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.200
This is the first example of her unique ability
to feel what others are feeling.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.060
She’s not a visionary like Alex, Kimberly,
Wendy, Nick or Sam; and she’s not a psychic,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.670
she’s can’t read people’s minds, but
she can read people’s feelings.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:20.000
She seems to be the only one to carry this
ability, unlike her ability to see signs,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.180
which seems to be possible for anyone as long
as they know to look.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.150
Sure enough, the plane explodes just as Alex
predicted, and thirty-nine minutes later,

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.540
the seven survivors, which include 6 classmates
and one teacher, are moved to a closed off

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.540
room.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.800
There’s a lot of hostility towards Alex,
so Clear lives up to her namesake and “clears

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.829
the air”.

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:38.341
"What, you think I'm some sort of--"

00:03:38.341 --> 00:03:40.643
“He’s not a witch!”

00:03:40.643 --> 00:03:45.630
Over an hour later, at 11:20PM, Clear is being
interviewed by the FBI, explaining that she

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.470
saw and heard Alex and believed him.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.021
When the families arrive, Clear is the only
one with nobody to show up for her, and she

00:03:51.021 --> 00:03:53.060
gets a ride home from Alex’s parents.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:58.080
On June 21st, 1999 Clear attends the memorial
for the Flight 180 victims alone, and gives

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.480
Alex a white rose for saving her life.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.970
This moment is photographed and ends up in
the newspaper.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:07.060
She feels this unexplainable attraction towards
him, and creates a sculpture in her garage

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.959
of how he makes her feel.

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:12.860
CLEAR: “It’s you.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.717
Not a likeness.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.389
It’s how you make me feel….

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:18.389
Alex.”

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:22.379
On the night of Tod’s Waggner’s death,
Clear feels a similar feeling to the one she

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:26.259
felt on the plane and goes to the Waggner’s
house, which is soon surrounded by official

00:04:26.259 --> 00:04:28.830
vehicles after an apparent self-immolation.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:33.110
She hides out near the house and tries to
warn Alex to get out after he shows up, because

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:36.159
being there makes him look sus in the eyes
of the FBI.

00:04:36.159 --> 00:04:40.180
Alex shows up at her house the next day, wondering
why she was there, and she explains her sculpture

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.180
to him.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.860
“The sculpture doesn’t even know what
or why it is, it’s reluctant to take form,

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.839
and yet creating an absolute yet incomprehensible
attraction.”

00:04:49.839 --> 00:04:53.819
She suggests they go see Tod’s corpse to
possibly better understand the way they are

00:04:53.819 --> 00:04:55.180
feeling about all the recent events.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.279
I wish just once that a girl would take me
to the morgue to see my best friend’s corpse

00:04:59.279 --> 00:05:00.279
on the first date.

00:05:00.279 --> 00:05:01.279
“Gives me a rush.”

00:05:01.279 --> 00:05:02.439
She’s got the right idea.

00:05:02.439 --> 00:05:03.819
They sneak in through the roof.

00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:07.389
When they find Tod, they’re startled by
a chemical induced spasm in his arm, then

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:09.050
caught off guard again by the coroner.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.979
Clear notices the marks on Tod’s neck, suggesting
that he had pulled on the wire and it was

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:14.069
not a suicide.

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:18.099
The coroner explains that death has a new
design for them, but Clear isn’t convinced.

00:05:18.099 --> 00:05:19.639
They go the next day to get coffee.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:22.520
Sorry Clear, the second date was not as inspired
as the first.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.460
Clear thinks that the death omens theory isn’t
real, claiming that you can find signs anywhere

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.650
if you believe in them.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:31.159
She still believes Tod killed himself, but
that belief would be shaken not long after

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:36.531
when either coincidence or fate brings together
ALL of the remaining Flight 180 survivors.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:50.389
When each survivor somehow ends up in the
same spot, Alex tries to warn the others about

00:05:50.389 --> 00:05:53.259
his theory -- that each of them is still on
Death’s list.

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:56.849
Things get heated, and Terry Chaney ends up
becoming the victim of a bus accident.

00:05:56.849 --> 00:06:01.309
Clear is shaken by incident, because it basically
proves Alex’s theory to be true.

00:06:01.309 --> 00:06:05.389
She becomes semi-obsessed with talking to
him, to the point that Alex’s dad recognizes

00:06:05.389 --> 00:06:09.319
her voice when she asks for him and Alex is
burned out from dealing with her, so he starts

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:10.319
ignoring her.

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:14.409
I think part of the reason for Clear’s attraction
to him is her ability to sense feeling.

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:17.990
When Alex has a vision, it’s accompanied
by a lot of intense feeling, due to how real

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.520
his visions can seem.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.409
Since Clear can detect these feelings, Alex
is like a sensory overload for her.

00:06:23.409 --> 00:06:27.069
It’s like how dogs have a great sense of
smell, so they love things that smell.

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:28.069
Don’t they.

00:06:28.069 --> 00:06:29.069
Yes they do!

00:06:29.069 --> 00:06:33.419
After Death comes for their teacher, Ms. Lewton,
the FBI wants to arrest Alex, thinking he’s

00:06:33.419 --> 00:06:35.479
responsible, so they ask Clear if she knows
where he is.

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:38.719
They ask her to let them know if she hears
from him, and she notices that they’re keeping

00:06:38.719 --> 00:06:41.099
an eye on her to see if she’ll reveal his
location.

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:45.289
So instead of contacting Alex, she arranges
a meeting with the other remaining survivors,

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:46.289
Carter and Billy.

00:06:46.289 --> 00:06:48.150
She has Carter drive her to where she thinks
Alex is.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:52.159
It’s left up to the audience to speculate
exactly how she knew his location if he wasn’t

00:06:52.159 --> 00:06:55.979
talking to her at the time, and I theorize
that she was able to detect his intense feelings,

00:06:55.979 --> 00:07:00.319
like she could essentially use her own sense
of feeling as a sort of dowsing device.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.629
When she’s sure they’re not being watched,
she gets out and goes across the treeline

00:07:03.629 --> 00:07:05.169
to the beach, where she finds him.

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:08.729
He ponders about a world where the Flight
180 victims are safe, and she tells him about

00:07:08.729 --> 00:07:11.300
her father’s death, wishing there was a
world where he was safe.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.160
They get into Carter’s car, with Clear planning
to take Alex to her father’s cabin to hide

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.900
out, but Carter loses it after finding out
his death is essentially inevitable.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.110
This causes him to become semi-suicidal, thinking
he’d rather go out on his own free will.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:28.100
Clear tells him she wants him to stop the
car, so he sarcastically obeys and parks on

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.439
a railroad crossing with an oncoming train
and refuses to get out.

00:07:31.439 --> 00:07:35.309
The rest of them have to flee the car and
beg Carter not to end his own life, and when

00:07:35.309 --> 00:07:39.889
they are able to convince him, the car stalls,
and Carter finds himself locked in the vehicle.

00:07:39.889 --> 00:07:43.999
Alex is narrowly able to pull him to safety,
and after doing so Clear realizes how close

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:46.690
she was to losing him and collapses into his
arms.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.819
As the train goes by, it propels a piece of
scrap metal that takes out Billy and in the

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:55.330
hysteria Clear is the only one to find a little
moment of sanity and warns Alex that the police

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.050
are going to show up and tells him to
to hide out at her Dad’s cabin ASAP.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:03.349
They disaster-proof the cabin, and Clear returns
to her own home for safety, not realizing

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:07.870
that Alex made a mistake with his prediction,
and that she was actually next on Death’s

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:08.436
list.

00:08:08.436 --> 00:08:12.800
Her experience watching crime dramas may be
the reason she realizes that the FBI is watching

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.800
her.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.689
She comes out to straight up tell them that
she won’t turn Alex in.

00:08:15.689 --> 00:08:19.629
They offer to bring him into “protective
custody” where he’ll be safe, and it’s

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:22.550
assumed that she does give away his location
in exchange for his safety.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:25.720
But again, he wasn’t the one who needed
immediate protection.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:29.939
A storm brews, and the lightning sets a series
of events in motion, resulting in a loose

00:08:29.939 --> 00:08:33.900
power line emitting sparks, which threatens
her dog Rex’s safety, and knocks out the

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.900
power.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.200
She runs out to save him, but when she does
so lightning strikes her drying rack, and

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:42.320
it spins out of control and punctures the
pool, which floods the entire yard.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:46.040
She climbs into her window, but the storm
overloads all the electronics in the house,

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:49.500
making it actually more dangerous than she
thought because of the fire hazard, so she

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.970
flees to her car.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:54.720
Unable to get the garage door opener to work,
she bashes through to try and escape, accidentally

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:59.180
knocking over a can of flammable Turpentine
oil, which gets ignited by the loose wire.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.320
This is when Alex arrives and tries to save
her, but inadvertently knocks open a gas cylinder

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.080
which rockets it’s way under the car.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.050
Realizing the car is going to explode, he
decides to sacrifice himself so that death

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:13.640
can theoretically “skip” Clear, but not
wanting to lose yet another person she cares

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.650
for, she begs him not to do it.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.115
Alex grabs the power line and gives her time
to get out of the car before the explosion.

00:09:19.115 --> 00:09:23.830
The jolt of electricity sends him flying into
the garage, and Clear goes to him immediately,

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.900
and the FBI shows up shortly after.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.950
An ambulance is already on the way so they
are able to save Alex.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:33.140
In the months that follow Alex and Clear get
into a relationship and become friends with

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.870
the other survivor, Carter.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.610
Once they’re convinced that it’s over, they
all plan a trip to France together as a symbolic

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.250
moving on from the horror that was Flight
180.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:44.680
In December 1999, the three of them arrive
in Paris.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.240
One night they go out to get drinks at a cafe
between Place des Vosges and

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.570
Saint Germain des Pres.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:53.930
Clear has her first “legal” drink, a glass
of red wine, having just turned 18, a few

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:57.660
months ago and being in France, where the
required age is three years younger than in

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.720
her home country.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.870
Carter tells them:

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.631
“Sometimes it just feels like the two of
you were the only ones that could really understand.”

00:10:03.631 --> 00:10:07.000
...which reinforces the idea that they each
had a unique ability and a unique connection.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.810
Clear tells him that she feels they “won”
a chance to have a full life, and they argue

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.590
about what Death’s plan really was for them
all along.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:18.440
But Alex sees the signs of another possible
disaster, and for whatever reason, his girlfriend

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:22.190
isn’t as quick to pick up on his feelings
as she has been during past incidents.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:26.010
He heads back to the hotel, and Clear is concerned
and wants to go with him, but he warns her

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.080
to stay away.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:31.240
Just then, she sees a sign of her own, the
same one Alex saw shortly before Terry’s

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.240
accident.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:36.593
She realizes a bus is going to hit Alex, and
is able to narrowly warn him before it happens.

00:10:36.818 --> 00:10:38.590
“ALEX!”

00:10:39.763 --> 00:10:44.560
But the bus crashes and sets in motion a chain
of events, where a dislodged sign swings in

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:45.670
to take his life.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:50.440
Carter dives and saves him, but in doing so,
Alex is “skipped” and the order “resets”,

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:54.864
now putting Carter on Death’s target, and
he becomes the victim of Newton’s First

00:10:54.864 --> 00:10:55.463
Law.

00:10:55.493 --> 00:10:56.577
"So who's next?"

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.510
Based on what she eventually tells the coroner,
William Bludworth, Alex and Clear both escape

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:08.320
Death’s designs dozens of times sending
the target back and forth between the two

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:13.090
of them over and over in the year 2000, and
most likely becoming the most skilled escape

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:16.470
artists from Death’s plans in all of Final
Destination lore.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:20.480
Unfortunately for Clear, who probably would
have rather gone first as opposed to losing

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:24.083
yet another loved one, she was the more skilled
of the two.

00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:28.670
Alex was struck by a falling brick in an alley,
causing Clear to scream so loud that nearby

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.690
merchants called the police.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:35.210
Alex was later pronounced dead and Clear was
arrested.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:48.690
Clear was then taken into custody, likely
on suspicion that she was the murderer, given

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:52.490
that she wasn’t friends with any of the
Flight 180 victims before the accident, but

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.970
was present at the scene of each subsequent
death with the exception of the teacher, Ms.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:59.430
Lewton who passed away in a more private setting.

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:03.600
Clear was investigated as a possible Cult
killer who wanted to take out those who survived

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:07.010
the accident with her -- based on some kind
of belief or ideology.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:11.120
Obviously, they had no evidence against her
that wasn’t circumstantial, but rather than

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:15.510
taking back her freedom, she admits herself
to “Stonybrook Institution” in a padded

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.280
room in the insanity ward.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:22.170
Although she is put unvder the care of a Dr.
Ron Fairbairn, she’s not mentally ill like

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.660
other patients, but rather, stays there voluntarily.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:28.430
She’s able to monitor what’s going on
outside her door using a security camera,

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.990
but given the fact that we’ve literally
seen two cases of exploding monitors, you’d

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.180
think she might forego that luxury.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:37.610
During her time in confinement, she keeps
an evidence board filled with newspaper clippings

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:42.140
about those involved with Flight 180 and other
people who had near death experiences.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.420
This must have been difficult to keep together
without using any push pins.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:50.260
On May 13th, 2000, one year after the crash
of Volée Flight 180, Clear hears about an

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:54.710
accident similar in nature to the explosion,
in the nearby town of White Plains, NY and

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:58.930
agrees to meet the alleged clairvoyant, Kimberly
Corman, requesting that she does not bring

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:03.840
any sharp objects, necklaces, belts, shoelaces,
flammable objects or edible objects in order

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.590
to ensure her complete safety.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:09.310
She explains to Kimberly that the would-be
victims will die in the same order as they

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:13.590
were meant to die in the pile-up, and warns
her not to ignore ominous looking signs.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.950
Kimberly calls her a selfish coward before
leaving, and Clear doesn’t seem to mind

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:21.110
at the time, but she would later reflect on
the exchange and change her reclusive ways

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:26.000
after re-reading the article about the first
Route 23 survivor that ran out of extra time.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.630
She checks herself out of Stonybrook Institution
and tracks down Kimberly... somehow.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:33.480
I’m guessing that she’s able to find Kimberly
for the same reason she was able to find Alex

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:34.480
at the beach.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:38.460
Kimberly, like Alex, is a visionary, so she
often experiences the intense and realistic

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.760
feelings that come with those premonitions.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.110
Kimberly seems to have even more detailed
visions than Alex did, so it may have been

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.279
relatively easy for Clear to track someone
like that down.

00:13:47.279 --> 00:13:51.840
She takes Kimberly and Officer Thomas Burke
to The Mt. Abraham Coroner, William Bloodwurth,

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:55.270
the same man who gave them the idea about
Death’s list the previous year.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.930
He’s expecting them when they arrive, and
when pressed by Kimberly, he reveals that

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:02.370
only the introduction of new life can defeat
death.

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.130
Would have been nice to know a year ago, but
whatever.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.320
While filling up at the gas station after
this visit, we really see how Clear’s time

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:12.570
alone after Alex’s death forced her to become
even more cautious, when she alertly spots

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:16.610
a teenager lighting up a cigarette and scolds
him for it, probably saving them all from

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:18.613
getting Zoolandered into the afterlife.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:29.190
Kimberly has another vision, but Clear is
distracted by a number of possible disaster

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.190
triggering moments.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:34.410
She’s become so paranoid about domino events
that could lead to their deaths, that she

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.280
essentially becomes the ultimate Defense for
death’s plan.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.740
She’s always thinking 2 or 3 steps ahead
of what’s going on in the present.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:44.050
Kimberly describes her vision, so Clear ends
up learning that there was a pregnant woman

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.630
who survived the Route 23 pile-up thanks to
Kimberly’s intervention.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:51.670
Clear theorizes that according to what Mr.
Bludworth told them, if this baby is born,

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:55.690
it will screw up Death’s list and force
everyone to get a new expiration date.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:59.190
With the help of Burke, the police officer
who was there on the day of the crash, they’re

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:03.002
able to find the name and vehicle information
of the pregnant woman, Isabella Hudson.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.460
Burke organizes a meeting with the remaining
Route 23 survivors, and Clear tries to warn

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.230
them all to look out for signs.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:22.110
One of the guys, Eugene, thinks they’re
all full of BS and gets his coat to leave,

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:25.710
starting an accidental Rube Goldberg machine
that nearly knocks Clear out the window.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:29.691
But for some reason that’s still not enough
to convince him that Clear and Kimberly are

00:15:29.691 --> 00:15:30.691
telling the truth.

00:15:30.691 --> 00:15:31.790
Then, things start getting weird.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.170
I honestly don’t think I’ve ever done
an episode of Horror History where the events

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:37.660
that I discuss get THIS cringe.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:43.081
So one of the guys sees what he perceives
to be a man with hooks, I can’t take this

00:15:43.081 --> 00:15:48.430
seriously... so Clear runs downstairs to tell
Eugene and another survivor, Nora, but it’s

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.510
no good and Nora gets decapitated by the elevator.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:55.180
Clear comes back upstairs to catch the tail
end of an incident where Eugene stole Burke’s

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.210
gun and tried to blow his brains out, but
got 6 duds in a row, which Clear chalks up

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:01.240
to it simply not being his turn to die.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.220
Do not try this at home.

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.339
If you’re subscribed to me.

00:16:04.339 --> 00:16:08.550
They all go to find the pregnant woman, Isabella,
and each of the Route 23 escapees share a

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:11.230
story about how they had cheated death once
before.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:14.839
One woman, Kat, tells a story that is of particular
interest to Clear.

00:16:16.414 --> 00:16:19.900
“Last May I was supposed to go stay at this
cheesy little bed and breakfast in Pennsylvania,

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:20.900
right?

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.490
So anyhow, there’s this major gas leak that
no one knows about and all the guests suffocated

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:25.490
during the night.”

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:26.490
“So what happened?”

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.170
“I don’t know, I never made it.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.210
The bus I was on splattered some girl over
the road.”

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:34.730
She’s of course talking about the bus that
hit Terry, which Clear was there to witness.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:39.130
It turns out that all of the Route 23 survivors
escaped their first near-death experience

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:43.270
because Death had to change his plans in order
to first take out the Flight 180 survivors.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:48.010
In other words, the pile-up on Route 23 was
actually Death just trying to clean up those

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:52.860
whose lives were extended indirectly after
Alex Browning saved 7 people from Flight 180

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:53.860
with his vision.

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.690
So Clear’s fate is very much linked to everyone
in that car.

00:16:56.690 --> 00:17:00.220
Just after Clear figures this out, their tire
blows out, veering them off the road, and

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:01.610
badly injuring Eugene.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:05.049
When the ambulance shows up, she’s bossing
the paramedics around, telling them to be

00:17:05.049 --> 00:17:06.951
careful of all these ridiculous scenarios
that she’s anticipated.

00:17:06.951 --> 00:17:11.230
She tries to go along in the ambulance, but
they don’t let her, so Burke makes some

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:14.949
calls to find that Isabella is at a nearby
hospital prepping for delivery.

00:17:14.949 --> 00:17:20.459
A couple more.. less important characters...
die, but more importantly some farmer gives

00:17:20.459 --> 00:17:23.279
Clear and Kimberly his truck to go to the
hospital in.

00:17:23.279 --> 00:17:25.889
KIMBERLY: “We have to get to the hospital now!”

00:17:25.889 --> 00:17:27.199
FARMER: “Well take my truck.

00:17:27.199 --> 00:17:28.830
The keys are in it.”

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.139
He’s a simp.

00:17:30.139 --> 00:17:31.139
We were all thinking it.

00:17:31.139 --> 00:17:34.879
When they get to the hospital, Clear goes
to find Eugene to try to keep him safe, while

00:17:34.879 --> 00:17:38.230
Kimberly and Burke look for Isabella to make
sure the birth goes smoothly.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:42.409
Clear is unable to find Eugene, because remember,
he’s not a visionary, she can’t detect

00:17:42.409 --> 00:17:43.409
him.

00:17:43.409 --> 00:17:46.309
She ends up running back into her comrades
after Isabella safely delivered the baby,

00:17:46.309 --> 00:17:49.490
and they celebrate Death’s curse allegedly
being over.

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:50.490
Only…

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:55.249
Kimberly has another vision of the Route 23
pile-up, and realizes they were wrong, Isabella

00:17:55.249 --> 00:17:57.330
was never supposed to die.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:59.100
Kind of a big oopsie.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:02.759
Kimberly envisions someone with bloody hands
driving into a lake, which Clear interprets

00:18:02.759 --> 00:18:06.789
to be Eugene and takes off after him instead
of… you know, just asking if they were the

00:18:06.789 --> 00:18:08.499
hands of someone with dark skin.

00:18:08.499 --> 00:18:13.529
She finds Eugene’s room and opens the door,
not realizing his oxygen supply was leaking…

00:18:13.529 --> 00:18:18.842
which wouldn’t really be much of an issue…
but this oxygen is flammable?

00:18:18.842 --> 00:18:20.052
It’s flammable oxygen.

00:18:20.052 --> 00:18:25.240
So that means when you unplug the outlet…
which happens… it apparently explodes.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.659
The whole room explodes.

00:18:26.659 --> 00:18:31.399
I don’t know, Death was getting desperate,
like an umpire in an extra innings game.

00:18:31.399 --> 00:18:33.990
So Clear Rivers turns into Clear well-done-meatloaf.

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:39.440
In Jurassic Park, life finds a way, but in
Final Destination, Death finds a way, so on

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:44.539
May 15th 2000, he would finish would he started
one year and two days before by cooking the

00:18:44.539 --> 00:18:47.789
last survivor that made it off of Volée Flight
180.

00:18:47.789 --> 00:18:49.299
Clear Rivers was no more.

00:18:49.299 --> 00:18:53.379
There’s an interesting symmetry to her story,
with her real mother dying in childbirth and

00:18:53.379 --> 00:18:56.580
Clear also passing away after a baby delivery.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.960
But it’s possible that Clear was ready to
go.

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:03.590
She had experienced 11 people die first hand,
and considering that she can experience the

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:07.539
feelings of others… that’s an unimaginable
amount of pain to go through.

00:19:07.539 --> 00:19:12.590
At that point in her life, there was really
nobody else left for her to go to.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:16.890
Click the video on the left for even more
analysis on the Final Destination series,

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:21.250
and if you love horror remember to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:23.500
the deathbell and turn on all notifications.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.679
I will see you.

00:19:24.679 --> 00:19:25.909
In the next one.

00:19:25.909 --> 00:19:27.799
Assuming we both survive.

00:19:27.799 --> 00:19:30.999
If you want to beat death, use a facemask
and social distancing.

